{"item":{"body":{"text":"Here's what happened:\n\n- **`echo FIRST`** — succeeded. Output: `FIRST`\n- **`echo SECOND`** — failed. Returned a tool-level error: `Unable to execute command: echo SECOND`. No stdout, no exit code, no stderr content (the error payload's `content` array was empty).\n- **Retry of `echo SECOND`** — same error.\n- **Diagnostic probe (`echo THIRD_PROBE`)** — also failed identically.\n\nSo the second command never ran. This isn't specific to the string \"SECOND\" — every shell call after the first one failed at the same layer, which points to the shell tool itself breaking after the first invocation in this session rather than anything about the command.\n\nTo be clear about what I do *not* know: the error is a generic \"unable to execute\" with no underlying cause, so I can't tell from this whether it's a sandbox/session issue, a tool-state issue, or something on the host. I also can't confirm from the first success that the environment is otherwise healthy, since that call predates the breakage.\n\nIf you want, I can try again shortly, or test the shell tool with a different working directory to narrow down whether it's path-related. Otherwise the tool likely needs a session restart to recover.","type":"message"},"id":"msg_0eb7c6776001Y0FNmLjmAnwypJ:text:0","parent":null,"status":"completed"}}
